From 99f9dcce57761e86fe9f78267b01c5428d5bd188 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John <326213404+jedeyesniv-art@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:14:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Point sprites at the game's size, scaled with the
 internal resolution

OpenGL ignored a vertex shader's PSIZE (GL_PROGRAM_POINT_SIZE was never
enabled) and only applied the GXM point/line width when it changed, so
every point was one pixel at any resolution: TxK's particle effects
(power-ups, scores, the starfield) were nearly invisible. The draw now
enables program point size for shaders that write PSIZE and sets the
fixed size (width x res_multiplier) otherwise. The translated PSIZE is
multiplied by a new vertex uniform res_multiplier (OpenGL and Vulkan).
Shader cache version 15 -> 16.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
