 ## Unreleased
 
+- Point sprites are drawn at the size the game gives them, scaled with the internal resolution. On OpenGL a size set by the vertex shader was ignored (GL_PROGRAM_POINT_SIZE was never enabled) and the point/line width was applied only when it changed, so every point was one pixel at any resolution (TxK lost most of its particle effects); on Vulkan the shader's size was not scaled with the resolution. The shader cache is rebuilt once (cache version 16).
 - What the user makes is kept in RetroArch's save directory, which can be synced to cloud storage, in its `vita3k` folder laid out as the Vita's storage, wherever Storage Location puts the rest: the accounts with their saves, trophies and play times (`ux0/user`), the photo album (`ux0/picture`) and the registry (`vd0/registry/system.dreg`). What the core's folder still has there (from earlier builds, or a standalone Vita3K folder copied in) is moved over at the next start or reset, shown as Moving data, merged with what the save directory has: a file it already has stays where it was, with a warning in the log. Remove Content's saves and trophies option and Remove Account delete them there. `ux0/data`, where homebrew and ports keep their game files, stays in the core's folder (sco8487).
 - The registry works: the core never started it (upstream does so from its GUI), so every sceRegMgr call of a game ran on an empty one, reads finding nothing and writes being dropped. Its template comes with the firmware, and `system.dreg` is made from it when missing (sco8487).
 - Storage Location: the other location is now `vita3k` in RetroArch's download directory (Download Directory), no longer in its save directory, whose small files get uploaded to cloud storage and which is no place for installs; nor the cache directory, which RetroArch empties. A storage still in the save directory is moved to the download directory at the next start, shown as Moving data, and the option set to Download Directory (#7, i30817).
diff --git a/vita3k/renderer/src/gl/draw.cpp b/vita3k/renderer/src/gl/draw.cpp
